+## 10. Online evaluation after training (optional for setup)
+
+Offline training and Zarr conversion do not need RLBench, PyRep or CoppeliaSim. For closed-loop success evaluation, use the single-arm setup in the original `README.md`. A separate evaluation environment avoids disturbing your working training environment:
+
+```bash
+conda create -n 3dfa-ndf-eval --clone 3dfa-ndf
+conda activate 3dfa-ndf-eval
+python -m pip install open3d
+mkdir -p "$HOME/robotics"
+cd "$HOME/robotics"
+git clone https://github.com/stepjam/PyRep.git
+cd PyRep
+wget https://www.coppeliarobotics.com/files/V4_1_0/CoppeliaSim_Edu_V4_1_0_Ubuntu20_04.tar.xz
+tar -xf CoppeliaSim_Edu_V4_1_0_Ubuntu20_04.tar.xz
+export COPPELIASIM_ROOT="$PWD/CoppeliaSim_Edu_V4_1_0_Ubuntu20_04"
+export LD_LIBRARY_PATH="${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:-}:$COPPELIASIM_ROOT"
+export QT_QPA_PLATFORM_PLUGIN_PATH="$COPPELIASIM_ROOT"
+python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
+python -m pip install -e .
+cd ..
+git clone -b peract https://github.com/MohitShridhar/RLBench.git
+cd RLBench
+python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
+python -m pip install -e .
