+
+These simulator commands follow the uploaded README's Ubuntu20.04 binary setup; other Linux distributions can require additional Qt/OpenGL system libraries. Install Xvfb on an Ubuntu machine if absent (`sudo apt-get update` then `sudo apt-get install xvfb xauth`). Export the CoppeliaSim variables in every evaluation shell. The simulator setup has not been exercised here.
+
+Return to the delivered repository root and evaluate:
+
+```bash
+CHECKPOINT=/absolute/path/to/your/best.pth \
+CHECKPOINT_ALIAS=push_buttons_ndf \
+DATA_DIR=peract_raw/test \
+TASKS="push_buttons" \
+  bash online_evaluation_rlbench/eval_peract.sh
+```
+
+New checkpoints contain architecture/camera settings and frozen NDF weights. The patched evaluator restores them before selecting the environment cameras and loads new-format state dictionaries strictly. This prevents accidental evaluation with the four-camera CLI default when training used `PeractTwoCam`. The evaluation shell script itself remains unchanged; avoid spaces in its path environment variables because the original script does not quote all expansions.
